{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "KJV1769",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 7,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD my God, in thee do I put my trust: save me from all them that persecute me, and deliver me:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lest he tear my soul like a lion, rending ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in pieces, while ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none to deliver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD my God, if I have done this; if there be iniquity in my hands;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have rewarded evil unto him that was at peace with me; (yea, I have delivered him that without cause is mine enemy:)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let the enemy persecute my soul, and take ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it;",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " yea, let him tread down my life upon the earth, and lay mine honour in the dust. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Arise, O LORD, in thine anger, lift up thyself because of the rage of mine enemies: and awake for me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the judgment ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou hast commanded.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So shall the congregation of the people compass thee about: for their sakes therefore return thou on high.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD shall judge the people: judge me, O LORD, according to my righteousness, and according to mine integrity ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh let the wickedness of the wicked come to an end; but establish the just: for the righteous God trieth the hearts and reins.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My defence ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of God, which saveth the upright in heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God judgeth the righteous, and God is angry ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with the wicked",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " every day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If he turn not, he will whet his sword; he hath bent his bow, and made it ready.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath also prepared for him the instruments of death; he ordaineth his arrows against the persecutors.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, he travaileth with iniquity, and hath conceived mischief, and brought forth falsehood.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He made a pit, and digged it, and is fallen into the ditch ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he made.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His mischief shall return upon his own head, and his violent dealing shall come down upon his own pate.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:PSA.7.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will praise the LORD according to his righteousness: and will sing praise to the name of the LORD most high.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
